 "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you? You've got the most important one, curiosity. Show an interest in what she's learning, and ask open ended questions. It is. A simple I don't know can lead to her asking the teacher in class, which is a great learning skill. Then ask her about it at bedtime. What did you like today? What were you confused about? She might at first, but consistency matters. A short, regular tradition shows her you value her learning. Set aside time together each evening, and use games that tie into the topics. She'll love it, and it' stick with her much longer than facts taught in class.",
